# Testing And Acceptance

This root is an orchestration repo, not a unified app workspace. Do not invent `npm run typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, or `build` at the root; those scripts do not exist here.

App commands live in each nested app repo. See `docs/ecosystem-root-runbook.md`.

## Root fast validation

- `node scripts/dev-workflow/inspect-repo.mjs`
- `node --test scripts/dev-workflow/verify-workflow-setup.test.mjs` when workflow files change
- `node scripts/validate-ecosystem-contracts.mjs` when contracts change
- Targeted `node --test` for the scripts you touched

## Root implementation validation (only if the change needs it)

- `npm run validate:ecosystem-contracts`
- `npm run supabase:validate` for shared Supabase work
- `npm run proof:security-static` for auth/RLS/service-role boundaries
- `npm run proof:ecosystem:static` for static ecosystem proof

## App validation (run inside the app repo with that app's package manager)

XFlow, Verixet, AudAix, RatAiFy: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, `npm run build`.

WordGeni, CreVux: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`.

## Reporting

Use PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED, NOT RUN, or MANUAL VERIFICATION REQUIRED. Do not downgrade a failed gate to declare a phase complete. Compiling is not completion.
